      "about": "Its corners round to its target's.",
      "viewport": [48, 36],
      "steps": 8,
      "from": {"box": [8.3, 6.6, 28.4, 20.7], "fill": [0.2, 0.4, 0.8, 1], "corner_radius": 0.8, "opacity": 1},
      "to": {"box": [8.3, 6.6, 28.4, 20.7], "fill": [0.2, 0.4, 0.8, 1], "corner_radius": 9.6, "opacity": 1}
    },
    {
      "name": "fill",
      "about": "Its colour and alpha change to its target's.",
      "viewport": [48, 36],
      "steps": 8,
      "from": {"box": [8.3, 6.6, 28.4, 20.7], "fill": [0.9, 0.2, 0.3, 0.5], "corner_radius": 4.2, "opacity": 1},
      "to": {"box": [8.3, 6.6, 28.4, 20.7], "fill": [0.2, 0.6, 0.8, 0.95], "corner_radius": 4.2, "opacity": 1}
    },
    {
      "name": "opacity",
      "about": "It fades in to its target's opacity.",
      "viewport": [48, 36],
      "steps": 8,
      "from": {"box": [8.3, 6.6, 28.4, 20.7], "fill": [0.2, 0.4, 0.8, 1], "corner_radius": 4.2, "opacity": 0.15},
      "to": {"box": [8.3, 6.6, 28.4, 20.7], "fill": [0.2, 0.4, 0.8, 1], "corner_radius": 4.2, "opacity": 0.9}
    },
    {
      "name": "everything",
      "about": "Every value moves at once, over a backdrop that does not. The element starts inside its target, in a colour nearer the target's than the backdrop's.",
      "viewport": [48, 36],
      "steps": 8,
      "backdrop": {"box": [0, 0, 48, 36], "fill": [0.95, 0.94, 0.9, 1], "corner_radius": 0, "opacity": 1},
      "from": {"box": [17.3, 12.4, 14.2, 9.5], "fill": [0.35, 0.55, 0.7, 0.8], "corner_radius": 1.4, "opacity": 0.8},
      "to": {"box": [14.8, 10.6, 24.6, 17.9], "fill": [0.2, 0.5, 0.8, 0.95], "corner_radius": 6.3, "opacity": 0.95}
    }
  ],
  "zero_gradients": [
    {
      "name": "no-overlap-with-the-target",
      "about": "A square-cornered element and its target do not touch. Moving it changes which pixels differ and not how much, so position has no gradient. Neither has a corner radius of zero: rounding a square corner a little takes away an area that grows as the radius squared. Size, fill and opacity have one.",
      "viewport": [64, 36],
      "elements": [
        {"box": [5.3, 8.45, 14.6, 12.27], "fill": [0.2, 0.4, 0.8, 1], "corner_radius": 0, "opacity": 0.9}
      ],
      "target": [
        {"box": [40.7, 14.3, 14.6, 12.27], "fill": [0.2, 0.4, 0.8, 1], "corner_radius": 0, "opacity": 0.9}
      ],
      "element": 0,
      "zero": ["x", "y", "corner_radius"],
      "non_zero": ["width", "height", "fill", "opacity"]
    },
    {
      "name": "rounded-without-overlap",
      "about": "The same with rounded corners. An arc is drawn as its tangent, so the element's whole cover changes a little with where its corners fall among the pixels, and position has a small gradient that the shape itself does not: a limit of this renderer, measured here.",
      "viewport": [64, 36],
      "elements": [
        {"box": [5.3, 8.45, 14.6, 12.27], "fill": [0.2, 0.4, 0.8, 1], "corner_radius": 3.1, "opacity": 0.9}
      ],
      "target": [
        {"box": [40.7, 14.3, 14.6, 12.27], "fill": [0.2, 0.4, 0.8, 1], "corner_radius": 3.1, "opacity": 0.9}
      ],
      "element": 0,
      "zero": [],
      "non_zero": ["x", "y", "width", "height", "corner_radius", "fill", "opacity"]
    },
    {
      "name": "under-an-opaque-element",
      "about": "The element lies wholly under a later opaque one, so nothing about it reaches a pixel.",
      "viewport": [48, 36],
      "elements": [
        {"box": [12.4, 9.3, 14.6, 10.2], "fill": [0.9, 0.3, 0.2, 0.8], "corner_radius": 2.2, "opacity": 0.9},
        {"box": [6.2, 4.1, 30.5, 24.6], "fill": [0.2, 0.4, 0.8, 1], "corner_radius": 0, "opacity": 1}
      ],
      "target": [
        {"box": [20.7, 14.3, 14.6, 10.2], "fill": [0.9, 0.3, 0.2, 0.8], "corner_radius": 2.2, "opacity": 0.9},
        {"box": [9.6, 6.3, 30.5, 24.6], "fill": [0.2, 0.4, 0.8, 1], "corner_radius": 0, "opacity": 1}
      ],
      "element": 0,
      "zero": ["x", "y", "width", "height", "corner_radius", "fill", "opacity"],
      "non_zero": []
    },
    {
      "name": "no-opacity",
      "about": "The element has no opacity, so nothing about its shape or colour reaches a pixel; its opacity does.",
      "viewport": [48, 36],
      "elements": [
        {"box": [8.4, 7.3, 20.6, 14.2], "fill": [0.9, 0.3, 0.2, 0.8], "corner_radius": 3.2, "opacity": 0}
      ],
      "target": [
        {"box": [12.7, 9.3, 20.6, 14.2], "fill": [0.9, 0.3, 0.2, 0.8], "corner_radius": 3.2, "opacity": 0.9}
      ],
      "element": 0,
      "zero": ["x", "y", "width", "height", "corner_radius", "fill"],
      "non_zero": ["opacity"]
